    "title": "Marketplace small fixes: the post cap, business payment wording, Orders photos for the profile picture",
    "why": "Follow-ups from the Nov 1 UI/UX review (ux-review.md) still open in the live code, approved by Jason in chat. (1) At the 5-post cap (0135 §7), Post it on Your Marketplace and Post something on /market/ are greyed out with the reason (a team member's test post doesn't count, so ticking Test post frees it). (2) A business item with Buy now no longer says no payment passes through the site; Your Marketplace's intro and the FAQ say a person's posts are paid between you, a business's items to the business itself. (5) A photo chosen from the Gallery's Orders catalog reached the profile picture's cropper as an empty file; it now carries the photo, and the server still copies the order's own file. The 'More skips posts' finding was already fixed by paging by number (2026-11-12). FAQ: the cap, paying, and the Orders catalog.",
